ers\n2. Alphabetical tie-break among libraries with equal dependency depth: `pkg/format` (f) < `pkg/sys` (s) < `pkg/testutils` (t)\n3. `cmd/version` (consumer of infrastructure) comes last\n\nThe single permitted task is **pkg/format** implementation (rel00.0-uc002-format).\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Task\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format column alignment, ANSI color, and size conversion (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component; design_decisions DD3; technology_choices)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (use case -- contains reference to the pkg/format PRD; read the referenced PRD before writing any code)\n      - go.mod (module path and Go version)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/table.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment type and tabular output formatting functions\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI escape-sequence constants and file-type color helper functions\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte-count-to-unit-string conversion\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement column alignment for tabular output per the pkg/format PRD: accept a [][]string grid and per-column alignment hints; return padded rows suitable for writing to stdout\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement ANSI color support per the pkg/format PRD: return escape-sequence-wrapped strings for each supported file-type class (regular file, directory, symlink, executable, etc.)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement human-readable size formatting per the pkg/format PRD: convert a uint64 byte count to a K/M/G string using the 1024-based thresholds and decimal precision defined in the PRD\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"pkg/format must have no external dependencies beyond the Go standard library -- no golang.org/x/sys, no cmd/ imports, no third-party packages\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read the pkg/format PRD referenced in docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml before creating any files; derive exact exported type names, function signatures, and file names from the PRD, not from inference\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Name each source file after its primary exported type per planning convention P7 (e.g., if the column type is named Table, the file is table.go; if the PRD uses different names, use those names exactly)\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"pkg/format must not import golang.org/x/sys or any package outside the Go standard library; only pkg/sys may use golang.org/x/sys per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology_choices -- pkg/format uses stdlib only\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/... completes with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"golangci-lint ./pkg/format/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Column alignment returns rows where each cell is padded to the correct width with the correct alignment (left or right) as specified in the PRD\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"ANSI color helpers return strings that begin with the correct ANSI escape sequence for the given file-type class and end with the terminal reset sequence\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Size conversion output matches PRD-specified thresholds: values at and above each K/M/G boundary use the corresponding unit suffix\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"All exported identifiers in pkg/format carry Go doc comments (required for golangci-lint to pass with revive or godot linters)\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21268,"cache_read_input_tokens":13920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21268},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standar